==Question #3==
{{Cquote2|Can you tell us a bit more about the projects which were presented in your last Game Jam? We’d love to know which if any were green-lighted to go further. Also, were there any that didn’t get a response you had hoped for, but you think would be a significant contribution to the main game?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHS1F5tx9xU&t=358s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Ash:''' One of them has already been launched, from me. What I pitched were the additional modes for Last Man Standing that we'd always said could be made to support alternate modes. I'd hoped that would happen last year, but it got a new map instead at the time.
* '''Mod Ash:''' I finally had a week that I could just go and programme it.  We couldn't do the whole thing in the week, it's not that small an update! But it was a great time to get most of the infrastructure in place, and much thanks to Mod Goblin for working with players to help get feedback on the loadout. I'm very pleased that we got that one out there. It was a small update but a lot more variety for the mini-game as a consequence.
* '''Mod Ash:''' In terms of the other projects, Tasakaal Trials got a really good response from what I've seen, and I very much hope that's going to be able to go forward. It won't be this year - you can kind of guess that from the fact it's October - but we think that will be a very good one to put to the players.
* '''Mod Ash:''' Also, a special call out for Soff with the Wilderness; it's a massive expansion! That's a big one; frankly, we think pulling that one off is a very tall order. Beyond the work we're doing with the bosses at the moment - and hopefully another Bounty Hunter next year - I'd like us to be able to look towards something of that scale. I think the area deserves it, and there's a lot in there that players can have a lot of fun with.
* '''Mod Ash:''' There was some good skilling stuff as well. Forestry stands out as one that could well turn up next year as a skilling update so that it is not all bashing things. We hope to get more of them in there. Of course, just because we pitch something at Game Jam doesn't mean that it's definitely going ahead. Maybe the next Game Jam will pitch an even better idea that we should do instead of it. There are always more ideas and players with ideas. It's been a while since we saw a Community Design Competition.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' So, we have the combat achievements interface, which is very pretty. You can filter your tasks by criteria like bosses, difficulty, etc.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' With the Achievement Diaries, you get a little fake quest scroll from way back instead of anything useful. There is a disparity in the technology that also plays to the backend systems where it's not exactly pretty to add, remove or update any of the tasks because that task list is from basically when it launched.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' It's a shame because we've released a lot of good content since then. So, it'd be nice to encourage players to experience that content for the first time. Also, if we make you do different tasks, it makes sense to update the rewards simultaneously and maybe change some of them so that the teleports are consistent.
* '''Mod Bruno:''' As for me, I'd really want to work on Taskaal Trials. That looks like a really fun piece of content. Also, the Dog Quest... We need a Dog Quest in RuneScape!
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I'm going to echo the Dog Quest. It's less about the quest and more about the fact that I want pet dogs of various kinds! Dog Quest is a good way to get them!
* '''Mod Kieren:''' Dog Quest seems to have become the official name at this point. Gertrude's Dog, right? It stuck with us.
* '''Mod Ash:''' I think the title "Dogs of Gielinor" would work quite well because our projects tend to have a newer code prefix. Like Tombs of Amascut was ToA, Chambers of Xervic could have been CoX. "The Dogs of Gielinor" would have been the prefix of the DOG, which works quite well.
* '''Mod Light:''' I was gonna say Dog's Quest, too. I'm a really casual player, so it appeals to me so much. We can't really talk about what projects we're going to be taking further because, as I mentioned, there's going to be a summit-style stream where we'll talk a bit more about our roadmap, but Dog's Quest is my personal favourite.

==Question #4==
{{Cquote2|Can the Jar of Darkness drop rate be looked at again? The previous poll failed by 3%, presumably partly because the 1/500 rate that was polled was still too rare for some voters. Also, when is the next content Poll coming out?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHS1F5tx9xU&t=734s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Light:''' We have good news! This particular topic is going to be brought up in Poll 77, and it's coming up relatively soon. So, adjustments will be made to the rate that the Jar of Darkness drops. It will be polled. No adjustments will be made until it passes the poll, as well as the stale baguette, which we know is something that has come up a lot in player feedback.
* '''Mod Light:''' More information is going to be in the Poll 77 blog. I don't have an ETA for you on that. We expect it to come as soon as the team has finished giving feedback on it, and it's gone through all our usual processes.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I think it's an awkward one because it's tradable. It has a price associated with it. There's some prestige with players who have got it. These ones are always difficult, because we feel like we probably made a mistake. We made the Jar of Darkness too rare, given how you interact with Skotizo getting the totems.
